<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU agrees limits on pesticide residues in food.</title>
<headline>EU agrees limits on pesticide residues in food.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers agreed by qualified majority on Tuesday to adopt common pesticide residue limits in food, despite German objections stemming from worries over the treatment of baby foods, EU officials said.</p>
<p>Germany, along with Sweden and Denmark, had voiced objections because of concerns over baby food imports from other member states, where standards were lower than their own.</p>
<p>The new rules, which cover cereals, fruit, vegetables and food products, harmonise pesticide levels in member states and introduce an EU-wide system of control.</p>
</text>
